question Gear_m1.5_N17 (G1): A bore cannot be added to or removed from a built part through its values, so it needs a new part. Build again as Reducer_12to1_r2? That makes new parts for G1 (Gear_m1.5_N17_r2) and G2 (Gear_m1.5_N69), reuses 2 parts that have not changed and makes a new layout part and assembly (Reducer_12to1_r2_Layout and Reducer_12to1_r2.SLDASM). G2's part is new because Gear_m1.5_N68 has changes from Update SolidWorks that are not saved; to reuse it instead, answer No and save it in SolidWorks first (if SolidWorks has closed it since without saving, those changes are gone, and it cannot be reused). Nothing is overwritten, and Reducer_12to1.SLDASM stays as it is on disk, but it shares the 2 reused parts: a later Update SolidWorks that changes one of them changes Reducer_12to1.SLDASM too.
footer  (structural, unsaved) [green] Gear_m1.5_N17 (G1): A bore cannot be added to or removed from a built part through its values, so it needs a new part. Update SolidWorks offers to build again as Reducer_12to1_r2. It was built with its gears mated to turn: drag G1 in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. Gear_m1.5_N68, Reducer_12to1_Layout and Reducer_12to1 have changes from Update SolidWorks that are not saved: save them in SolidWorks to keep them. If SolidWorks closed them without saving, those changes are gone. While Gear_m1.5_N68's changes are not saved, the new revision makes G2's part new, as Gear_m1.5_N69, rather than reuse it.
